21:["$","$L3e",null,{"faqs":[{"question":"What is cloud migration?","answer":"Cloud migration is moving your applications, data, and infrastructure from on-premise servers — or from one cloud to another — onto a cloud platform like AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud. Depending on the workload, you rehost it as-is, replatform it with targeted upgrades, or refactor it to run cloud-native."},{"question":"What are the main challenges of cloud migration?","answer":"The usual ones: hidden dependencies between systems, surprise costs after go-live, downtime risk during cutover, data security and compliance, and skills gaps in the in-house team. We de-risk each with a fixed-scope assessment, dependency mapping, waved cutovers, and FinOps from day one."},{"question":"How long does a cloud migration take?","answer":"It depends on the number and complexity of workloads. A single app can move in weeks; a full datacenter exit runs months, in waves. We scope it in the discovery phase so you get a realistic timeline and cost before any migration starts."},{"question":"How much does cloud migration cost?","answer":"Engineering starts at $50 USD/hour with senior certified talent, and the engagement is scoped up front. Just as important is what migration saves: right-sizing and FinOps frequently cut the ongoing cloud bill enough to offset the project cost."},{"question":"AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud — which should we choose?","answer":"It depends on your stack, your team's skills, and your workloads — not on who we resell (we're vendor-neutral). We assess fit across all three and recommend the platform, or mix, that costs less and runs better for your case."},{"question":"Will there be downtime during migration?","answer":"We plan for zero-downtime cutovers wherever possible — migrating in waves, running old and new in parallel, and switching over with validated rollback plans. Any unavoidable maintenance window is scheduled and minimized."},{"question":"What are the steps in a cloud migration strategy?","answer":"A proven cloud migration strategy runs in five steps: 1) assess your on-premise infrastructure, costs, and dependencies; 2) plan the approach per workload (the 7 Rs) and the target architecture; 3) migrate in waves with zero-downtime cutovers; 4) optimize cost with FinOps; 5) operate and keep improving. We scope steps 1–2 as a fixed-price assessment."},{"question":"What are the 7 Rs of cloud migration?","answer":"The 7 Rs are the standard options for each workload in a migration: rehost (lift-and-shift), replatform (lift-and-optimize), refactor (rebuild cloud-native), repurchase (move to SaaS), relocate (move as-is at the hypervisor level), retire (shut it down), and retain (leave it where it is — for now). Most portfolios mix several."}],"id":"faq","title":"What teams ask before migrating.","fill":true}]
22:["$","section",null,{"data-reveal":true,"className":"border-b-hairline-soft py-20","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-mono text-label uppercase text-fg-muted [letter-spacing:var(--tracking-label)]","children":"Related services"}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"mt-4 font-display text-display-m font-bold text-fg","children":"Often paired with cloud"}],["$","ul",null,{"data-reveal-stagger":true,"className":"mt-8 flex flex-col gap-4","children":[["$","li","data-analytics",{"children":"$L3f"}],["$","li","custom-software-development",{"children":"$L40"}],["$","li","ai-automation",{"children":"$L41"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-20 font-mono text-label uppercase text-fg-muted [letter-spacing:var(--tracking-label)]","children":"Learn more"}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"mt-4 font-display text-display-m font-bold text-fg","children":"From the blog"}],["$","$L42",null,{"posts":[{"title":"AWS vs Azure vs GCP: which cloud for your migration?","slug":"aws-vs-azure-vs-gcp","category":"Guide","excerpt":"AWS vs Azure vs GCP comes down to fit, not hype. AWS has the widest service catalog, Azure wins on Microsoft estates, GCP leads on data and Kubernetes. Here's how to pick the right cloud for your migration.","readMin":5,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/cloud-aws-azure-gcp-hall.webp","imageAlt":"Rows of glowing server racks in a data center, comparing AWS vs Azure vs GCP for a cloud migration"},{"title":"The real benefits of cloud migration, with numbers","slug":"benefits-of-cloud-migration","category":"Guide","excerpt":"The benefits of cloud migration aren't abstract — they show up as lower run cost, faster releases, and less downtime. Here are the real numbers behind each one, and how to know which benefits actually apply to your workloads.","readMin":5,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/cloud-benefits-technician.webp","imageAlt":"Data center technician among colorful server cabling, representing the benefits of cloud migration"},{"title":"Cloud cost optimization: a FinOps 101 guide to stop overpaying","slug":"cloud-cost-optimization-finops","category":"Guide","excerpt":"Cloud cost optimization is how you stop the bill from running you. This FinOps 101 guide covers where the waste hides, the levers that actually move spend, and the operating model that keeps it down.","readMin":6,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/cloud-finops-optimization.webp","imageAlt":"Technician inspecting efficient server racks, representing cloud cost optimization and FinOps"},{"title":"Cloud migration challenges (and how to avoid them)","slug":"cloud-migration-challenges","category":"Guide","excerpt":"The most common cloud migration challenges — runaway costs, downtime, security gaps, and scope drift — and a practical, step-by-step way to avoid each one before it derails your move to the cloud.","readMin":7,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/cloud-challenges-cables.webp","imageAlt":"IT engineer untangling network cables in a server room, illustrating cloud migration challenges"},{"title":"Cloud migration strategy: a step-by-step playbook","slug":"cloud-migration-strategy","category":"Guide","excerpt":"A cloud migration strategy is the plan that turns moving to the cloud from a gamble into a sequence. Here's the step-by-step playbook — assessment, the 6 Rs, sequencing, cost control, and the pitfalls that sink most migrations.","readMin":6,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/cloud-migration-strategy-aisle.webp","imageAlt":"Technician walking a data center aisle between server racks, executing a cloud migration strategy"},{"title":"Lift-and-shift vs re-architecting: which migration approach?","slug":"lift-and-shift-vs-re-architecting","category":"Guide","excerpt":"Lift and shift vs refactor: lift-and-shift moves apps to the cloud as-is for speed; re-architecting rebuilds them cloud-native for long-term cost and scale. Here's how to choose the right migration approach for each workload.","readMin":6,"date":"Jun 2026","image":"/blog/covers/cloud-lift-shift-install.webp","imageAlt":"Technicians installing a server into a rack, illustrating lift-and-shift vs re-architecting migration"}],"className":"mt-8"}]]}]
